From f14c135d42e94b14a636d67be67a0407ad8e9922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:52:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(owner-forward): a receipt naming an admission is
 unconfirmed, never a resendable "did not admit it"

PR #2265 review (t_01a1d52389d67d1f, review 5892083689), point 1 (behaviour): the owner's
prompt.submit receipt carries status queued/started/terminal, but AdmissionReceipt.status also
allows "unknown". A receipt outside the confirmed states raised OwnerUnavailable("the gateway did
not admit it") even when it named an admission_id, and #2265 made that error transient: the paused
continuation would be forwarded again under a fresh submission_id, queueing a second copy behind a
durable row the owner already holds. The Desktop submit path said "Nothing was sent. Send it again"
for the same receipt.

Now a receipt that names an admission but no confirmed state raises OwnerUnconfirmed (never
retried; the pause retires with "it may be queued there", the Desktop gets
SESSION_OWNER_UNCONFIRMED). Only a receipt naming no admission stays the transient "did not admit
it". Today's SessionAuthority._receipt reports the freshly inserted row, so this was latent.

Point 2 (wording): the docstring and WARNING said the 30 s backoff "retries" the forward. It only
gates the next try, which the next resume, boot sweep or refused-turn retry makes; the WARNING now
says "kept for a later try after the 30s backoff".

Tests: new test_a_receipt_naming_an_admission_is_never_resent drives the real forward_prompt and
relay (fake owner discovery/socket only). RED without the owner_forward change (the admission-named
receipt was forwarded again), GREEN with it. 30 related files (update_pause*, auto_continue,
owner-forward consumers, gateway prefix pin): 424 passed. scripts/check --base origin/main: 19 ok.
---
